From 2c51e29ee241636f7087969dfb7c8a1cdcb888cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-perf <perf@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:14:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] x86: precise flag-walk for the shipped cmp->test
 zero-compare fold

dead_writes.rs rewrites `cmp $0, mem` to `test $0, mem`, which changes
ONLY AF, and guarded that with flags_reach_a_whole_flags_reader.  That query
used walk_flag_consumers with preserved=0, so the walk stopped at ANY writer
-- including stc, which writes CF and nothing else.  A whole-word reader
sitting behind one was never examined:

    cmpq  $0, (%rax)      ; -> testq: AF diverges
    je    .Lkeep          ; ZF only: allowed, queues .Lkeep
    jmp   .Lout           ; the walk's fall-through leaves here
.Lkeep:
    stc                   ; writes CF only  -> walk stops
    lahf                  ; reads SF ZF AF PF: MISSED

`lahf` observes precisely the flag the fold changes, so the rewrite was
licensed on a path where it is observable.  This is a LATENT defect in
existing shipped code, not in the new fold -- the same walker, the same
coarse model.

flags_reach_a_whole_flags_reader_except_af and
flags_reach_an_sf_consumer_preserving_zf_cf_pf_of take the preserved set from
what the caller actually proved:

  whole-word query  preserved ZF|CF|SF|OF|PF   (AF is the divergent one)
  SF query          preserved ZF|CF|PF|OF     (SF is NOT provably identical
                                                in the branch that calls it,
                                                so SF and AF are both out)

sahf writes SF and AF, so it still terminates both walks; stc writes CF and
is stepped over; cld/std write no EFLAGS arithmetic flag and are stepped
over.  The originals are untouched and every other caller keeps preserved=0,
so no other pass changes.

COST: zero.  Compiled 935 programs under tests/ before and after: 0 produce
different assembly.  This is a correctness fix that costs no optimisation at
all, which is the only kind worth landing.

EVIDENCE: a_cf_only_setter_does_not_hide_a_lahf_from_the_zero_compare_fold
asserts the coarse query returns FALSE on that input and the precise one
returns TRUE -- i.e. it demonstrates the bug rather than merely the fix.  Its
complement asserts the precise query does NOT veto when nothing reads AF, so
this is a precision fix and not a blanket refusal.  Every label in all three
tests is real: an unresolvable branch target sets proved=false and vetoes for
the wrong reason, which is how a test of this shape passes vacuously.

cargo test --lib: 3910 passed, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
